A callback function in JavaScript is a function that is passed as an argument to another function and is executed after the completion of that main function.

***Example***
```js
function displayPopup () {
	alert("Hello!");
}
SetTimeout(displayPopup(), 200);
```
But what if you aren't going to use `displayPopup` anywhere else? Well, then it's better to avoid using a global identifier, so do this instead
```js
SetTimeout(function() {alert("Hello!")}, 200);
```
